# Drafted by Gemini (side quests batch 2: folk), edited.

~ tamsin_start
Narrator: A young woman in ink-stained cuffs taps a brass nib against a tall ledger, frowning at the wainscoted ceiling.
tamsin_ledger [neutral]: State your names and dates of decease for the parish rolls. I am auditing Wickermoor's municipal assets, and the bookkeeping is frankly irregular.
* Ask what she audits -> tamsin_audits
* Ask about the oak -> tamsin_oak
* Leave -> END

~ tamsin_audits
tamsin_ledger [weary]: From turnip tithes to that screaming timber on the Round, all in triplicate. Listing six public beheadings under seasonal pruning is a clear misallocation of county funds.
-> tamsin_start

~ tamsin_oak
tamsin_ledger [neutral]: The Oak of Many Faces lacks an arboricultural permit and refuses to sign a declaration of sap. I served its lower branches notice to vacate by the third bell.
-> tamsin_start

~ gaunt_start
Narrator: By the water trough, a whiskered veteran polishes a dented breastplate with a clump of dry hay.
sgt_gaunt [smile]: Stand at ease, travellers, before the hero of Bramble Ford. When bog-hounds breached the dyke, I executed a brisk four-mile tactical retreat to preserve my strategic judgement.
* Ask about his battles -> gaunt_battles
* Ask whether he'd help us -> gaunt_help
* Leave -> END

~ gaunt_battles
sgt_gaunt [sly]: At Hollow Pike I outran three phantom riders, and at Crooked Fen I held a turnip cellar from inside for forty hours. Only damp ground kept me from a glorious stand.
-> gaunt_start

~ gaunt_help
sgt_gaunt [smile]: Say the word and old Gaunt marches at the very front of the rear column. Wait, did that hay-wain creak? Draw your steel while I guard your backs from behind the trough.
-> END

~ pip_start
Narrator: A knee-high boy sits on the cold well-curb, rattling a tin cup of horn, bone, and brass buttons.
pip_oakum [smile]: Mind the puddle, strangers, you will splash the stock. Keep your soft silver; nothing holds a coat or a bargain together like a four-hole bone button.
* Ask what he collects -> pip_buttons
* Give him a copper for a button -> pip_deal
* Leave -> END

~ pip_buttons
pip_oakum [sly]: This pearl one fell off Postmaster Mayville's cuff, and the pewter hare is from Mayor Somerton's Sunday waistcoat. Constable Squire still owes me two brass anchors from her greatcoat.
-> pip_start

~ pip_deal
gold -1
Narrator: He bites your copper to test the metal, then solemnly presses a chipped wooden toggle into your palm.
pip_oakum [smile]: That is genuine ash-wood off Undertaker Shade's third-best gaiters, slightly stoat-chewed. Spend it wisely; you hold prime Wickermoor currency.
-> pip_start
